1
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too,

3
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I go chasing some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
in Katsushika, sighs and yawns,
nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water spout,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the evening sun sinks toward the great sky.

10
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
In Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost again.

12
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,540
I only realized after hearing it,
because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,600
Honda, Hayato, I'll gladly take it!

14
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,140
Alright, go on, Honda.

15
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,760
There, all cleared up now.

16
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,580
You can forget about Yoko-chan, right?

17
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:14,977
Yoko, Yoko-chan,

18
00:02:15,027 --> 00:02:16,340
How come?

19
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,780
Enough already, stop blubbering.

20
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:21,040
A man should forget a woman who dumped him,
just like that.

21
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:24,040
Yes sir, I'll forget all about Hayato Honda!

22
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,120
Alright, old man, the bill.

23
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:26,700
Here you go!

24
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:30,380
It comes to thirteen thousand yen.

25
00:02:30,380 --> 00:02:34,140
Next, in honor of Honda-san,
who surpassed Ryo-san's heartbreak record,

26
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:36,480
just ten thousand yen, that's it.

27
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,840
Thanks, sorry about that.

28
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,640
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait a second!

29
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:42,880
Did I really end up getting
dumped more times than you, senpai?

30
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:44,200
Well, well, I suppose.

31
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,260
It's no use.

32
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,660
I don't think I can go on
living as a human being.

33
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,320
Look, you're making it worse,
old man, saying unnecessary things.

34
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,940
S-sorry, Ryo-san.

35
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,540
Honda, don't get depressed.

36
00:02:58,540 --> 00:03:01,900
My count of failed romances only
starts from when I joined the police.

37
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:05,180
If you include the ones since I was a kid,
it's more than double that.

38
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:07,640
You're still just a
greenhorn compared to me.

39
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,740
Really?

40
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:09,060
Yeah.

41
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,540
Good, I feel a little braver now.

42
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:14,560
Shall we go for another round?

43
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:17,780
Yes! Let's go all the way tonight!
All the way!

44
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,100
He's getting into it, this guy!

45
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,420
Look, look!

46
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,920
Isn't that Honda-san! That's amazing!

47
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:34,820
Even though the one who got
dumped is working this hard...

48
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:39,960
And the one who was comforting
him ends up like this...

49
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,840
Shut up!
I've been drinking nonstop since then!

50
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,820
I got dragged along by the
Chief and lectured endlessly,

51
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,760
so why don't you take a
page from Honda-san's book?

52
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:55,200
He's throwing himself into
work to forget his breakup...

53
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:55,940
Naive.

54
00:03:55,940 --> 00:04:00,220
When Honda's fired up about work,
that's when he's in love.

55
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:04,360
He sinks fast,
but he bounces back even faster.

56
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:05,000
Well then,

57
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:08,040
he's definitely in love.

58
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:14,400
Heh.

59
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,280
Aaaaaah.

60
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:30,580
You think you can just run off now?

61
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:34,380
This isn't just any business, you know.

62
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:34,720
Damn it.

63
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:36,820
Sounds good.

64
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,020
Hey, stop it.

65
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:54,360
What kind of business is this?

66
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:55,480
Run, quick!

67
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:58,040
You think you can get away?!

68
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,760
W-whoa, you're going too far!

69
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:03,540
Senpai Honda!

70
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:04,780
How was it? Good work!

71
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:08,920
We've got a call from the Kōen-mae
police box asking you to come right away!

72
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:09,960
Got it!

73
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,380
Leave the rest to me!

74
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:13,180
Yes!

75
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:19,380
Damn that bastard! He really went all out!

76
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,780
I'll write a letter to
the newspaper about this!

77
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,780
Did something happen?

78
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,460
Nothing, sorry.

79
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:30,000
Make sure you properly cooperate
with the questioning, got it?

80
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,520
Scarier than the mob.

81
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:44,000
So, how did it go, senpai?

82
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:47,620
You're in love again, aren't you?

83
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:50,900
In the end, it works out well for you.

84
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:55,380
In your case, when you mope around and can't get over it,
you throw yourself into work.

85
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,600
That's right.

86
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,060
So, which girl is it this time?

87
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:05,010
Actually,

88
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:09,460
there's a motorcycle shop in Azabu
that does maintenance on Hakubai bikes,

89
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,800
and I fell for a woman who
works there at first sight...

90
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,060
Alright, then let's go.

91
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:18,840
It's better to settle things clearly
while the wound is still shallow.

92
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:22,340
W-well, that's like saying I've already been decided as the one who gets dumped,
isn't it?

93
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,420
Don't say "cram it in." It's
"go for it, even if you crash and burn."

94
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:26,160
I don't want to crash and burn.

95
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:31,500
Yeah, that's right.
Here, English, the rest is up to you.

96
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:38,080
What a big shop.
It's a motorcycle import company, you see.

97
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:45,160
Honguchi Motors is famous, you know. It's a
long-established nationwide importer of two-wheelers. I see.

98
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:53,540
I'm... wait, no, no.
I'm going home after all.

99
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:54,740
Tell me.

100
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:55,680
Just this once, barely.

101
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,600
Let's decide quickly, Honda-san.

102
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:03,680
Wow, it's all world-famous classic cars!

103
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:08,680
Recently they've been selling a large motorcycle
of their own make called the Motoguchi.

104
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:12,160
They're apparently aiming to become the
fifth-largest motorcycle maker in Japan.

105
00:07:13,080 --> 00:07:14,700
Looking forward to the future

106
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:17,680
Was she the woman who was there
at the Hakubai Itten-ken shop?

107
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,980
Then she's probably the company president's daughter,
I think.

108
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:24,820
The company president's daughter?

109
00:07:24,980 --> 00:07:25,220
Yes.

110
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:27,280
You fell for someone so far above you again

111
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:30,900
The daughter of a promising company's president,
and the son of a motorcycle repair shop.

112
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,400
Like the moon and a turtle, Honda.

113
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:36,980
Noooo, I'm going home,
going home, to my house.

114
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:37,380
Senpai.

115
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:40,260
Uh-huh,
so is that young lady here right now?

116
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:43,480
Yes, she's here. This way, please.

117
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:47,025
No way, I'm going home.

118
00:07:47,075 --> 00:07:49,420
Going home, I'm definitely going home.

119
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:55,380
Aaaaaaah.

120
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:04,340
The one riding right now is the young lady.
What a great ride, isn't it?

121
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:25,200
I'm Rika Motoguchi.
Can I help you with something?

122
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:30,080
This guy's a total knockout, isn't she?

123
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:30,920
Whoa -

124
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:33,680
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, you know.

125
00:08:34,340 --> 00:08:35,960
And this is Nakagawa. Nice to meet you.

126
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,680
And this one here is -

127
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:40,700
You're the motorcycle squad
officer who came by the other day,

128
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,640
you remembered us?

129
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,000
I'm touched.

130
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,100
From the Fourth Traffic Mobile Unit,

131
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:47,500
Hayato Honda, reporting!

132
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,700
So you're the famous Mr. Honda?

133
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,300
You know him?

134
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:54,540
You don't know about Honda,
the demon of the later years?

135
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,140
There aren't any riders in Tokyo like him.

136
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:58,760
Wow, you're nothing like

137
00:08:58,760 --> 00:08:59,400
what I imagined.

138
00:09:00,140 --> 00:09:02,260
I thought you'd be a much scarier person.

139
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:07,560
He's number one.
Well, he's like Jekyll and Hyde.

140
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:10,080
Honda, doesn't it look like
she's interested in you?

141
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,360
No, no, well.

142
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:16,380
By the way, Rika, this guy likes you.

143
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,780
Won't you go out with him, senpai?

144
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:24,080
Well, sure. Let's go out.

145
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,820
That's great, Honda!

146
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:27,460
Yes.

147
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:29,480
I'd gladly welcome that as friends.

148
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,240
As friends

149
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:31,820
Yeah.

150
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:38,120
Being "just friends" is a tricky thing.

151
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:40,180
It can also be taken as a polite
way of turning someone down.

152
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:42,980
But it's not a complete rejection, either.

153
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:44,800
The rest is up to your skill.

154
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:46,180
Let's go inside.

155
00:09:46,180 --> 00:09:46,820
Yes.

156
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,940
Wait, senpai.

157
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:51,980
What exactly does
"up to my skill" mean? What am I supposed to do?

158
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,940
Figure that out yourself.

159
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:55,280
That's easy for you to say.

160
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,460
There's no such thing as a simple answer.

161
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,180
In this case,
there's only one thing to do: go for it.

162
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,100
But...

163
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:00,960
No "buts," and no strikes.

164
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:05,860
Honda-san.

165
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:10,440
Are you all right, Honda-san?

166
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,040
I'm fine. This is nothing.

167
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:15,500
Senpai.

168
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:19,620
Don't worry about him. He's a guy who knows
how to tickle a woman's maternal instincts.

169
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,140
Nice going, Honda!

170
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:29,340
That's amazing!

171
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:30,520
Congratulations.

172
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:31,320
Honda-san.

173
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,700
Thank you very much.

174
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,260
Honda, this is a real marry-up opportunity.

175
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:36,100
Marry up?

176
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,080
It means marrying into a wealthy family.

177
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:40,200
She's an only child, right?

178
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:40,760
Yeah.

179
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,200
So if you propose to her

180
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,880
and manage to marry her,

181
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:51,280
you'll become the president
of Motoguchi Motors.

182
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:52,760
N-no way!

183
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:56,360
We've only just asked each other out.

184
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:59,700
If she agreed to a date,
it means she's interested in you.

185
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,980
A 50% chance of marriage?
Really? Is that so?

186
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:10,800
If that happens,
you owe thanks to me, the Cupid of love!

187
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:15,280
When you become president, you'll
give me a Ducati or Harley every month!

188
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:22,040
But you can't even ride them!
Selling them for pocket money every month?

189
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:28,000
At least make it one every two months! Don't be so petty.
If you hadn't brought it up, none of this would've happened.

190
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,680
It didn't go that smoothly, you know.

191
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:31,220
Well, that's true, but...

192
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:33,260
Alright, then, one every two months.

193
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:33,920
Yes.

194
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:37,300
And once I retire from the police force,

195
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:39,840
I'll bring you into the
company as vice president.

196
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:40,620
Got it?

197
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:41,860
Yes.

198
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:42,940
Alright, it's settled.

199
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,060
Yo, future big-shot president!

200
00:11:46,060 --> 00:11:46,600
Aw, come on.

201
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:04,200
Idiot! A date on a manual
bike like this won't cut it!

202
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,960
And I went to all the
trouble of researching it.

203
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:11,800
Pretending to be a city slicker won't work!
You need to show off your own personality!

204
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:16,700
M-my personality?

205
00:12:21,020 --> 00:12:23,880
When you're riding your bike,
you're brave and wonderful!

206
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,540
She's a pro rider too.
That won't work on her.

207
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:33,300
As for other personality
traits you could show off...

208
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,840
There's nothing.

209
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:37,140
Worried?

210
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:39,640
Actually, there is one. Don't worry.

211
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:41,900
Really?

212
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:45,600
Something Honda has that Motoguchi Rika doesn't:
a weapon.

213
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:46,860
That is,

214
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:47,800
That is,

215
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:49,660
he was born in the shitamachi.

216
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,480
Shitamachi-born.

217
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:55,800
As a master of the shitamachi,
I'll summon the shitamachi for you.

218
00:12:56,160 --> 00:13:00,060
Once you lure her into the shitamachi area you know like the back of your hand,
she can't escape.

219
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:01,340
Sounds like an antlion pit.

220
00:13:01,340 --> 00:13:04,020
Seeing the shitamachi, the birthplace
of Edo culture, for the first time,

221
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,160
she gets culture shock,

222
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,460
and ends up thinking Honda is wonderful.

223
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:09,340
I see.

224
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:10,800
Do you think so?

225
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:12,800
Then how about showing me around Asakusa?

226
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:15,740
Naive! Asakusa is far too mainstream.

227
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:18,680
Even a young lady like
her must already know it.

228
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:21,460
Then where should I take her?

229
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:22,640
Well, there's no helping it.

230
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:25,840
I'll set up the entire date course for you.

231
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:26,960
Senpai.

232
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:29,860
If you do exactly as I say,
everything will go smoothly.

233
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:31,840
Yes, I'm counting on you.

234
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,860
I'll make sure you become a company president,
you hear?

235
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:36,900
Just relax and leave it all to me,
like you're on a big ship.

236
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:39,040
I'm counting on you, senpai.

237
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,060
Namidabashi?

238
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,060
Isn't that kind of lame?

239
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:00,920
You idiot!

240
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:05,700
Namidabashi is where Joe and Tange Danpei first met,
isn't it?

241
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:09,740
But you explain that there's
actually no such bridge, and...

242
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,540
Cross Namidabashi backwards, Joe.

243
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:17,980
Do a Tange Danpei voice
impression to get some laughs.

244
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:20,900
As expected of a senior,
your bits are so detailed.

245
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,625
Joe! Yeah,

246
00:14:24,675 --> 00:14:27,700
Cross Namidabashi backwards!

247
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:29,040
Mom, what's that?

248
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:30,400
You mustn't make eye contact!

249
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,780
Is this really going to be okay...
like this...

250
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,940
Yes, this is Honda...

251
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:41,020
Rika-san?

252
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:41,680
Honda-san?

253
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:45,940
I'm sorry, but could we change our meeting
spot to the Sukiyabashi intersection?

254
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:47,480
W-well, that's...

255
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:48,100
Is that not okay?

256
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:50,340
No, I'll head there right now!

257
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:57,000
I can't do the Namidabashi
or Tange Danpei impression.

258
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:05,440
Next,

259
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,720
next is tandem riding on Motoguchi's bike.

260
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:09,820
Two-up riding will leave Rika swooning.

261
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:12,100
Once she's swooning,

262
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:14,140
it's Motoguchi's original bike.

263
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:15,900
Rika will happily hop on.

264
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,140
Then, *skasa*!

265
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:19,900
That exhaust note that stirs your heart

266
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,640
can only come from Motoguchi's bike!

267
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:24,220
No, Honda, you'll be swooning!

268
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:25,320
How was it?

269
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,860
Senpai, even I, a guy, got chills.

270
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:30,800
Then take notes, take notes!

271
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:31,240
Yes.

272
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:35,700
Who would have thought a line
like that would shake your heart,

273
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,720
only a pro can pull that off.

274
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:42,800
Sorry, Honda-san. I'm late.

275
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:47,040
Mifuyu-san, no, I wasn't waiting at all.

276
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:50,220
Good. Hey, shall we go in my car?

277
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,300
A cool car.

278
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:53,960
I'm blown away.

279
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,160
Where should we go?

280
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:00,880
Yeah, let me think.

281
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:07,960
Next is the meal.

282
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,780
Monjayaki, then?

283
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:10,620
Too sweet.

284
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:13,920
Monjayaki is too typical
and lacks any freshness.

285
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:16,420
If you want to give her culture shock,

286
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:18,900
make her eat wrapped
Japanese-style whale katsu.

287
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:22,360
Whale katsu... what's that...?

288
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,180
You don't know whale katsu?

289
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,240
It's whale tatsuta-age!

290
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,660
They served it at elementary school lunch,
didn't they!

291
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:32,360
It didn't come out, though.

292
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,420
I see.

293
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,360
We're from different generations, after all.

294
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,440
It's been over 12 years since the whaling ban,
so I guess it's understandable.

295
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:39,100
Sorry.

296
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,320
There's no need to give up.

297
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:42,320
Rika's younger than you, so...

298
00:16:42,320 --> 00:16:44,840
She probably doesn't even
know you can eat whale meat.

299
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,260
It'll definitely shock her.

300
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:48,180
I see.

301
00:16:48,180 --> 00:16:50,680
I see, so the meal is whale katsu.

302
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:54,280
About Rika and the meal...

303
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,340
Is this your first time eating Thai food?

304
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,960
Yes, it's my first time ever.

305
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,920
It's spicy, but it's delicious.

306
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:10,640
It's perfect, I'm good too.

307
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:11,800
Good.

308
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,920
Whale katsu was a bust too

309
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:21,080
After the meal, we'll go to Higashi-Mukojima
for a Shichifukujin pilgrimage.

310
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,860
And then there's the push-up
from the tugboat thing.

311
00:17:23,860 --> 00:17:25,820
You'll never find that in a manual.

312
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,940
That's the number two date course, you know.

313
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:30,000
Shichifukujin pilgrimage.

314
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,500
About what's next...

315
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:36,340
Let's go.

316
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,640
That was fun, wasn't it?

317
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:00,780
Yes.

318
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:03,120
I can't let it end like this.

319
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,920
I have to nail the ending.

320
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,420
On the way home from a date,

321
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,120
you walk the girl all the way home.

322
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,040
Show her you're a man of integrity.

323
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,160
Got it?

324
00:18:14,680 --> 00:18:15,640
Rika-san...

325
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,760
Well then, Rika-san. Today was really fun.

326
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:25,600
I'm glad you enjoyed it.
Well then, good night.

327
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,020
Good night.

328
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:41,140
Well, wow, it was my first time seeing and hearing all of that,
and I was so surprised.

329
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:43,620
What good is it if you're
the one getting culture shock?

330
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:46,885
Yeah, and on top of that,
she took me all the way to her home,

331
00:18:46,935 --> 00:18:48,120
and I was so nervous my heart was pounding.

332
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:50,420
She completely set the pace, didn't she?

333
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:51,560
S-sorry.

334
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,960
Wait, you did confess your love, right?
That's the most important part.

335
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:55,640
Huh?

336
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:56,600
You didn't?

337
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:57,280
Hah.

338
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:00,460
You idiot!
Then what was the point of going on a date?

339
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:04,700
But Rika had me meet her parents, you know.

340
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:09,560
What!? Her parents!? You got introduced
to her parents on your first date!

341
00:19:09,840 --> 00:19:10,160
Yes.

342
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:11,560
So, how did it go?

343
00:19:11,560 --> 00:19:13,920
Come on, Honda, have a drink.

344
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,020
Thanks.

345
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:19,100
I told them I was a Hakubai Corps member,
and her father took a real liking to me.

346
00:19:19,660 --> 00:19:20,600
Well done.

347
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:24,860
Getting in good with the father
is basically an 80% success.

348
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:26,360
Really?

349
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,440
That's right, isn't it.

350
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:31,700
Normally, when it's an only daughter,
the father is cold to her boyfriend.

351
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,400
You did it, Honda.

352
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:36,460
Don't forget about the president thing.

353
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,800
Leave it to me.

354
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:40,128
Alright, if you say "Shōin,"

355
00:19:40,178 --> 00:19:42,160
first, cut the horse clean in two.

356
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:44,280
Press the old man,
press him, press him hard!

357
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:44,920
Yes.

358
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:46,164
Actually,

359
00:19:46,214 --> 00:19:50,560
her father has invited me to come visit
his company on my day off this time.

360
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:55,240
This might be a 90% chance!
Good luck, Honda!

361
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:56,840
Yes!

362
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,440
By the way, what's become of Honda?

363
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:08,620
He found himself a nice girlfriend.

364
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:11,680
Come to think of it,
we haven't seen him around lately.

365
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:17,220
Nakagawa's off today, and yet he's here.

366
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:20,120
No, I've been worried about Honda too.

367
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:23,160
He's been missing for
a whole week since then.

368
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,260
Take care, Miss.

369
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:30,700
Everyone,
I'm counting on you to hold down the fort.

370
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,660
Yes, have a good trip.

371
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:39,040
Ryo-san and Nakagawa.

372
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:40,440
Where are you going?

373
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:42,120
I'm off to Europe for a while.

374
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,280
Europe.

375
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:46,340
I'll be racing road races over
there for about three years

376
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:48,820
to hone my driving skills.

377
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:53,000
Then what about your marriage to Honda?

378
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:57,640
Ugh, marriage? I have no intention
of getting married for a long time.

379
00:20:58,380 --> 00:21:00,840
Well, I might marry Ike, though.

380
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:03,880
Does Honda know about that?

381
00:21:05,540 --> 00:21:12,700
I tried, but Mr. Honda got caught by my father and I didn't have time.
Sorry, could you talk to the two of them for me? Well then.

382
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:22,480
And tell Mr. Honda let's go on another date when I'm back from Europe.
See you.

383
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:30,100
Aaaahhh!

384
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:37,780
Chief, Rika's traffic record
has been cut by two whole seconds!

385
00:21:37,780 --> 00:21:40,580
What? This is amazing data, President.

386
00:21:47,160 --> 00:21:48,380
Really big, isn't it.

387
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:49,840
I've still got plenty of go in me.

388
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:52,460
Well, well, that's most reassuring.

389
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:55,620
Then next,
I'd like you to test-ride this motorcycle.

390
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,440
Before that, please let me see Rika.

391
00:21:59,440 --> 00:21:59,720
Rika?

392
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:04,320
Uh-oh, if Honda finds out now,
development will be delayed again.

393
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,840
Rika is in the shower right now.

394
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:09,440
Shall we go and see together?

395
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:15,780
Now that I think of it, Rika said Honda
looks coolest when he's riding a motorcycle.

396
00:22:15,780 --> 00:22:17,120
Rika-san...

397
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:20,000
Honda, I'm off to do the test ride.

398
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,800
What on earth is going on?

399
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:26,240
That's just making him a mere test driver,
isn't it?

400
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:30,540
That reminds me, Honda said her
father took a liking to his skills.

401
00:22:30,540 --> 00:22:35,280
Hey, hey, isn't that a bit unfair to Honda,
Rika's old man?

402
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:36,300
Exactly.

403
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:37,800
Who are you lot?

404
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:39,540
We're friends of Honda's.

405
00:22:39,540 --> 00:22:43,960
Why are you keeping it a secret
that Rika left for Europe?

406
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:48,940
But you see,
Honda is a test driver our company needs.

407
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:52,780
Besides, I'm thinking of making him my son.

408
00:22:54,360 --> 00:22:55,960
So I'm marrying Rika?

409
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:58,180
Rika has nothing to do with this.

410
00:22:59,240 --> 00:23:02,180
Through an adoption, you'll become my son.

411
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:07,060
Then Rika and Honda would end up as siblings,
wouldn't they?

412
00:23:07,580 --> 00:23:10,820
That's right.
Is there some problem with that?

413
00:23:10,820 --> 00:23:12,220
It's over.

414
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:14,940
Oh no, not a problem at all.

415
00:23:14,940 --> 00:23:17,120
Mr. President, it's another course record!

416
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:17,940
What?

417
00:23:19,480 --> 00:23:19,920
Wait.

418
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:20,160
Wait!

419
00:23:20,360 --> 00:23:21,500
Senpai!

420
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:22,920
Never mind, never mind.

421
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:26,540
Still, we've secured a
post-retirement job, then.

422
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:27,400
No way!

423
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,480
Incredible ride, Honda.
Get the next machine ready.

424
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:32,120
Yes!

425
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:34,820
P-President, j-just a moment.

426
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:35,690
Oh yes, yes,

427
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:40,500
didn't your daughter also say she wants to
keep watching Mr. Honda ride his bike forever?

428
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:42,760
I'm on my way, Dad!

429
00:23:43,140 --> 00:23:46,011
Now then, Honda,
you're already as good as a son to me.

430
00:23:46,061 --> 00:23:47,780
Do your best.

431
00:23:48,140 --> 00:23:51,800
Senpai, either way,
we can't tell the truth, can we.

432
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:55,920
Poor guy. I guess I'll join him for
another drink to drown his sorrows.

433
00:24:03,620 --> 00:24:06,760
How dare those damn
mini-patrol girls pull this crap!

434
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:09,280
Making up whatever shit they want
and printing it in their articles!

435
00:24:09,640 --> 00:24:10,640
Just you wait.

436
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:15,100
I'll crush that worthless newspaper called
"Green Light" myself.

437
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:21,140
Next time: The Great Hot Car Newspaper War.
See you then.

438
00:24:30,660 --> 00:24:37,180
People gossip that I'm a
woman who can't fall in love,

439
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:42,760
but I have a mountain
of things I want to do.

440
00:24:44,300 --> 00:24:52,040
I want to ride my motorcycle
across a harsh desert.

441
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:59,400
I want to be freer than a bird.

442
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,060
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

